D-13: the T-H9/T-R19 tests assert on local model helpers, not production
code — and the model itself was WRONG: it assumed
ChatActivity.MODE_QUICK_REPLIES == 2, but production says 5 (2 is
MODE_PINNED). Production compares against the symbols everywhere, so
the wrong value never changed runtime behaviour, but it proves the
model tests cannot catch a renumbering. New AliGramPhase31PolicyTest
(plain JUnit, no Robolectric) asserts the PRODUCTION constants
(MODE_DEFAULT 0, MODE_SCHEDULED 1, MODE_PINNED 2, MODE_QUICK_REPLIES 5,
all distinct — compile-time constants, so no Android class loads at
runtime), the account-scoped blobIdFor overload (account 0 == legacy
id; other accounts get an 'a<N>_' prefix), and the distinct
NO_PIN_SOURCE reason. New AliGramPhase31DaoTest (Robolectric, real
in-memory Room, same harness as the sibling scope test) proves the DAO
contracts the fixes rest on: D-03 deleteRefsForAccountId deletes only
that account (and deleteRefsForAccount(0) — the logout bug's key —
deletes nothing); D-05 blob lookups are account-scoped for document
and photo keys; D-04 refreshSizeMtimeForPath fills in a PENDING row's
0,0 values and ignores DONE rows. No existing test file was edited.
Controller wiring (purgeAccount, copyForRef, release paths) is not
executable in this harness and stays verified by code review + CI.
